1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,950
Hey everyone, I'm Vikas.

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:05,900
I have over 3 years of experience

3
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:08,650
in startups and entrepreneurship.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:12,100
Here's one thing I've learned.

5
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:14,860
When I was in my initial phase,

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,780
building my own startup,

7
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:20,340
I thought funding was very easy.

8
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:21,600
I'd get it easily.

9
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:24,400
But then I got a reality check.

10
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,470
I realised how difficult funding is.

11
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:32,250
Investors bet on two things:

12
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,490
First, the founder.

13
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:36,070
Second, the company.

14
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:39,780
If the founder is really impressive,

15
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:42,530
from a strong college, investors may back them.

16
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:47,130
Or your startup is already in the market,

17
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:50,380
showing strong traction,

18
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:52,100
generating good revenue,

19
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:54,260
and has acquired customers.

20
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,000
So here's the issue:

21
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:00,930
If a founder is from a Tier 3 or Tier 4 city,

22
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:02,640
what should they do in that case?

23
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:04,020
They aren't from a good college,

24
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:05,830
they've only just started,

25
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:07,870
and have no funding to start with.

26
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:10,500
What can we do in that case?

27
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,270
Apply to accelerators.

28
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:15,030
There are many good accelerators.

29
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:18,090
You probably know

30
00:01:18,090 --> 00:01:20,860
one of the top accelerators:

31
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:22,450
Y Combinator.

32
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:24,490
Apply to such accelerators

33
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:27,080
if you're in the initial phase.

34
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:28,970
That's what I've learned.

35
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:31,670
Comment your point of view below.

36
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:32,620
See you in the next video.

37
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:33,480
Till then, bye-bye!
